dtfile: do not dereference a NULL datatype name list

ReadInFiletypes() walks the result of DtDtsDataTypeNames() without
checking it:

    file_types = (char **) DtDtsDataTypeNames();
    i = 0;
    while(file_types[i])          <-- NULL deref

DtDtsDataTypeNames() returns NULL whenever the data-attribute database is
unavailable -- get_da_db() returning NULL is an ordinary path in Dts.c,
not an assertion -- so dtfile dies on SIGSEGV reading address 0 before it
draws anything.  That is what "dtfile crashes on launch" looks like when
the datatype database has not loaded:

    TRAP: dtfile exception 14 -> signal 11 code 1 addr 0x0
    eax=0x00000000  code @eip: 8b 00   (mov (%eax),%eax)

With no type names there is nothing to filter, so return the same zero
count the normal path returns for an empty set.  Verified: dtfile now
reaches display setup and ToolTalk initialisation instead of faulting.

diff --git a/programs/dtfile/Filter.c b/programs/dtfile/Filter.c
index 76e05feb..1bbd5b3e 100644
--- a/programs/dtfile/Filter.c
+++ b/programs/dtfile/Filter.c
@@ -1488,6 +1488,20 @@ ReadInFiletypes(
    }
 
    file_types = (char **) DtDtsDataTypeNames();
+   /*
+    * DtDtsDataTypeNames() returns NULL whenever the data-attribute database
+    * is unavailable -- get_da_db() failing is an ordinary path in Dts.c, not
+    * an assertion -- and this walk dereferenced the result unconditionally.
+    * dtfile then died on SIGSEGV reading address 0 before it drew anything,
+    * which is what "dtfile crashes on launch" looks like when the datatype
+    * database has not loaded.  With no type names there is simply nothing to
+    * filter: leave the (already emptied) filter list alone and report a
+    * count of zero, which is what the normal path returns for an empty set.
+    */
+   if (file_types == NULL)
+   {
+      return(0);
+   }
    i = 0;
    while(file_types[i])
    {
